# Round XXVIII Track C POS fixture — verify ALLOW list is real (Core #15e Q3).
# Closure body tail with a direct top-level `!s` is a RESTING /
# consuming-boundary position (mirrors an expression-body fn tail). Must
# ACCEPT and RUN, printing "hello".
#
# Baseline for the "verify closure body tail suppresses" claim in the brief
# (Rust check_expr Closure arm now brackets `suppress_move_in_operand_position`
# when the body is a direct top-level `Expr::Move`; SH normalizes via the tail
# `SExpr(EMove(_))` suppress in `check_safety_stmts` — see the Round XXVIII
# Track C comment there).

void main():
    String s = "hello"
    Callable[String()] f = (): !s
    print(f())
